Z||000000||ordovician||12-18-2001||08:55 PM||||anyone know the bore size of the duke? exact size. i cant find it. also, is the rear end really 3.35, or am i mistaken. its an 87 with an L4||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||12-18-2001||09:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ordovician:<BR><B>anyone know the bore size of the duke? exact size. i cant find it. also, is the rear end really 3.35, or am i mistaken. its an 87 with an L4</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> The 2.5 has a 4.00" bore and a 3.00" stroke. Has a compression ratio of 9.0:1<P> The differential gear ratio in the 5 spd isuzu is indeed 3.35:1<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blacktree||12-19-2001||12:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Has a compression ratio of 9.0:1<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The 1984-86 engines had a 9.0:1 compression ratio, but the 1987 engine had a 8.3:1 compression ratio. Pontiac lowered the compression ratio so the engine could run on 87 octane (the 1984-86 required 91 octane).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
